# garbage collection

Returns every live object in lua heap. (tables, functions, userdata, strings, threads)

#### Credits <a href="#user-content-credits" id="user-content-credits"></a>

* Query, gc table and lock design based on `GcLib` by `.chloe`.

#### Examples

```lua
local objects = getgc()

print(#objects)                                  -- 10000 - 20000
print(objects[1].type, objects[1].address_hex)   -- userdata  0x2d00000
```

Filter by type:

```lua
getgc()                                      -- functions + userdata (default)
getgc(true)                                  -- getgc() + tables
getgc("string")                              -- strings only
getgc{ types = { "function", "table" } }     -- several types
getgc{ types = "userdata", limit = 500 }     -- capped
```

Read a string's contents:

```lua
for _, object in ipairs(getgc("string")) do
    print(gc.describe(object.address).value)
end
```

Group Instances by class, all Instances of a class share one metatable:

```lua
local classes = {}

for _, object in ipairs(getgc("userdata")) do
    local metatable = gc.describe(object.address).metatable_hex

    if metatable then
        classes[metatable] = (classes[metatable] or 0) + 1
    end
end
```

List C functions by code address, roblox strips function names:

```lua
for _, object in ipairs(getgc("function")) do
    local info = gc.describe(object.address)

    if info.is_c then
        print(info.func_hex, object.address_hex)
    end
end
```

Find a table by its keys and change it:

```lua
local gun = gc.first({ "Ammo", "MaxAmmo" })

if gun then
    print(gun.Ammo)      -- live read
    gun.Ammo = 999       -- live write
end
```

Count what is on the heap:

```lua
for type, n in pairs(gc.count()) do
    print(type, n)
end
```

